# Verify the remote build

After pushing Re_Call changes, inspect the GitHub Actions runs for that exact
commit and wait for the iOS Build workflow to finish. A local QC pass and an
iPhone installation do not establish that GitHub compiled the commit.

If the remote build fails, read its failed log and resolve the cause before
reporting all checks green. Keep local, physical-device, and GitHub results
distinct in completion reports. When adopting newer Apple APIs, explicitly
select a compatible Xcode in the workflow; runtime availability checks do not
make those APIs visible to an older SDK.
